[3.047668, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[2;35r\u001b[7S\u001b[r\u001b[H\r\u001b[7B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;80;80;80m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mScripted demo - follow EXACTLY, edit no files, do not improvise.\u001b[39m                                            \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mThe cwd is a compiled bleep repo (MAIN); its absolute path is `pwd`.\u001b[39m                                        \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m1. git worktree add -b seeded ../wt-seeded\u001b[39m                                                                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   git worktree add -b cold   ../wt-cold\u001b[39m                                                                    \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m2. Spawn two subagents IN PARALLEL: one message, two Agent calls, both in the\u001b[39m                               \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   FO"]
[3.047736, "o", "REGROUND. Do not background them and do not schedule wakeups - just wait\u001b[39m                               \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   for both to report.\u001b[39m                                                                                      \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   seeded: \"With the bleep MCP tools: call copy-state with\u001b[39m                                                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m     directory=<MAIN>/../wt-seeded and from=<MAIN>, then compile the same\u001b[39m                                   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m     directory. Report both results verbatim.\"\u001b[39m                                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   cold:   \"With the bleep MCP tools: call compile with\u001b[39m                                                     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m     directory=<MAIN>/../wt-cold. Do NOT call copy-state - this worktree\u001b[39m                                    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m     starts cold on purpose. Report the result verbatim."]
[5.049665, "o", "\"\u001b[39m                                                   \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m3. Both report historyId=1 in their own worktree. Ask bleep to compare the\u001b[39m                                  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   runs: history diff-timing with directory=<MAIN>/../wt-seeded, base=1,\u001b[39m                                    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   target=1, baseDirectory=<MAIN>/../wt-cold.\u001b[39m                                                               \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m4. Print, with real numbers from the tool results:\u001b[39m                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   agent[seeded]  copy-state: <bytes> bytes in <ms>  ->  first compile: success\u001b[39m                             \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   agent[cold]  "]
[5.049693, "o", "  first compile: success (compiled everything from scratch)\u001b[39m                                 \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   bleep history diff-timing (cold -> seeded): total <baseMs>ms -> <targetMs>ms\u001b[39m                             \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m   verdict: <one sentence with the ratio>\u001b[39m                                                                   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mThen stop.\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m·\u001b[3GImagining… \r\u001b[3B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[38;3H\u001b[?25h\u001b[?2026l"]
